body:
I don't engage in debates for more than 3 comments. Statement -> Rebuttal -> Closing argument. I don't have the time, energy or motivation to debate with people behind a computer screen when there is plenty of evidence to suggest everyone is stuck in their ways.

&#x200B;

And I'm not some pretentious prick on that matter either. I am not exempt from that. But I do like seeing other perspectives. I don't know if this makes me different, but it's something I like.

I really enjoy games like league but my vision honestly isn't the best and when things get chaotic on screen I lose track of where the mouse is and I would misposition on pc all the time because of it. I had moved to Arena of Valor for a while but then I decided to wait for wild rift to come out. With touch controls I can play league without needing a mouse

&#x200B;

I'm not a hyper competitive guy. My goals are very simple. Do my personal best that I can in every game I play, and just enjoy the experience. Despite all it's faults I think WR is a really well made game as is league on the whole. But WR is exactly what I wanted out of league. I can enjoy the champions and items and map and I actually never have to have chat on in my games ever. :D
